60,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, Anchor looks perfect! They have engineers on-site for rollout. That means they’ll fix our yard gear and train crews during the winter rush.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, on-site engineers are a capital expense the board will reject. I need a vendor whose contract structure stops the recurring fees from becoming our permanent financial cage.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, I reject that framing. Anchor’s on-site team enforces the stability we lack. Their presence prevents the scope drift that doomed our last project.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Rin,,"@Kenji, I love Anchor! But wait, if they use our old servers, won’t it just age quietly again? I need them to fix the messy handoffs, not just sit there!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, your caution is wise. Anchor’s engineers stay, but our people must learn. I worry if they leave, our thin team cannot sustain the knowledge.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, that’s a fair worry! But their engineers stay through the whole rollout. They’ll teach us everything before they leave. We won’t be left alone!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, presence is temporary. I need a contract that prevents the recurring fees from becoming our permanent financial cage.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, presence is temporary, but the process remains. Anchor’s on-site team enforces the stability we lack. Their presence prevents the scope drift that doomed our last project.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Mizuki, I get the money worry! But Anchor’s team fixes the messy handoffs. They won’t let the system rot like the old one.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Mizuki, the cage is real, yet so is the void left by departing administrators. Anchor’s presence bridges that gap, teaching our remaining staff before the engineers depart.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Mizuki, I hear you! But if the system crashes during peak season, we lose way more than fees. Anchor’s engineers keep us running.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, a crash is a symptom of the structural rot I documented. I will vote for Tessera, whose subscription model aligns with the operating budget the board actually approves.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, Tessera’s partner model is exactly the ambiguity I fear. Who is accountable when the workflow fails? I cannot vote for undefined ownership.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Mizuki, Tessera’s partner firm is just another outside team! Remember the 2018 mess? I won’t risk another broken handoff. I’m voting for Anchor!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,"@Mizuki, I understand the budget, but Tessera’s partner model leaves our people adrift. I vote for Anchor, whose engineers stay to teach our remaining staff.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Mizuki, I hear you, but Anchor’s engineers keep us running during the rush. I’m voting for Anchor to save our yards!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, I am voting for Tessera. Its subscription model aligns with the operating budget the board actually approves, preventing the capital rejection trap.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I vote for Anchor. Their on-site team enforces the stability and clear ownership we lack. We cannot afford another year of undefined accountability.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
